== S5: regrouping identity (geometric, block factor b) ==
  b=1 : fine plaquettes per block = 6*b^4 =     6 ; ln(6)=   1.792 ; b^2=1
  b=2 : fine plaquettes per block = 6*b^4 =    96 ; ln(96)=   4.564 ; b^2=4
  b=3 : fine plaquettes per block = 6*b^4 =   486 ; ln(486)=   6.186 ; b^2=9
  b=4 : fine plaquettes per block = 6*b^4 =  1536 ; ln(1536)=   7.337 ; b^2=16
  min fine plaquettes per touched block = 1 (a connected 'snake' through M blocks has |C|=M)
  => uniform per-block cost bound cannot exceed c0*q*1 ; block-graph entropy rate = gamma (isomorphic graph)
  => criterion invariant : gain exactly 0
  internal-config entropy ceiling per block: 96*ln2 = 66.5421 (b=2) ; ln C(96,48) = 64.0316

